 "text": "Hello there! How's life treating you? That's usually dry chain noise, not on the pedals. Is it wet where you ride? Apply little to each link, turn off the bike and miss few to lubricate. Or just use a dribble from your fingertip while turning? Peel off the seal and use a thin tool to apply it to one link, then turn the bike while it gets into the links. Clean it with a little oil, then apply it. For dry riding, yes. You don't want grease gripping the chain to the wheel. Just dry lube and forget the oil cleaning step.",
